{
  "id": "12-fabric-motion-refined",
  "title": "Build a Microsoft Fabric data agent \u2014 the three-step walkthrough",
  "script_sha256": "88481c00251be68b37dde150400d1ac341f314eb47eaf141c5281267c3af1c41",
  "duration": 84.0213,
  "beats": [
    {
      "scene": "hook",
      "text": "Your data is already in Microsoft Fabric. What if you could ask it a question, and inspect the query behind the answer?",
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 6.8373,
      "voice_end": 6.6773
    },
    {
      "scene": "preview",
      "text": "This is Microsoft's documented data agent example. A question goes in. An answer comes back, with the steps used to retrieve it.",
      "start": 6.8373,
      "end": 15.1253,
      "voice_end": 14.9653
    },
    {
      "scene": "steps",
      "text": "Here is the workflow. Create the agent. Choose its data. Then ask, inspect, and test.",
      "start": 15.1253,
      "end": 20.6827,
      "voice_end": 20.5227
    },
    {
      "scene": "create",
      "text": "In your Fabric workspace, select New Item. Search for Fabric data agent, select it, and give your agent a name.",
      "start": 20.6827,
      "end": 27.3707,
      "voice_end": 27.2107
    },
    {
      "scene": "sources",
      "text": "Next, add your data source from the OneLake catalog. That could be a lakehouse, a warehouse, or a Power BI semantic model.",
      "start": 27.3707,
      "end": 34.8907,
      "voice_end": 34.7307
    },
    {
      "scene": "tables",
      "text": "In Explorer, choose the relevant tables. Watch the checkboxes. You control which tables are available to the agent.",
      "start": 34.8907,
      "end": 41.8987,
      "voice_end": 41.7387
    },
    {
      "scene": "instructions",
      "text": "Add instructions that define your business terms. Tell the agent which source to use for different kinds of questions.",
      "start": 41.8987,
      "end": 48.288,
      "voice_end": 48.128
    },
    {
      "scene": "ask",
      "text": "Now ask a concrete question. Microsoft's example asks how many users played Contoso games, and how many users purchased items in those games.",
      "start": 48.288,
      "end": 57.6213,
      "voice_end": 57.4613
    },
    {
      "scene": "inspect",
      "text": "Here is the important part. Expand the steps and inspect the generated query. Check the filters, the tables, and the answer.",
      "start": 57.6213,
      "end": 65.312,
      "voice_end": 65.152
    },
    {
      "scene": "limits",
      "text": "A data agent can retrieve structured answers. A question about why sales changed needs more evidence. Retrieving a number does not prove its cause.",
      "start": 65.312,
      "end": 74.3467,
      "voice_end": 74.1867
    },
    {
      "scene": "close",
      "text": "Create. Choose. Verify. Start with one question you can check, then test more questions before you publish. That is a useful first Fabric data agent.",
      "start": 74.3467,
      "end": 84.0213,
      "voice_end": 83.8613
    }
  ],
